@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title Step lines — one renderer for init's apply, a run's start and teardown, and a line that leaves when a prompt arrives
' purpose: how a phase that runs things shows the step it is on, and what happens to that line when something else needs the terminal
' covers: internal/ui/steps.go
' covers: internal/ui/steps_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/init_apply.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/init_apply_test.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/tty_unix.go (openTerminal suspends the live line)
' covers: internal/choiceui/tty_windows.go
' covers: e2e/live_line_prompt_test.go
'   what a silent phase cost .......... _spec/_experiments/terminal-handoff-probes.puml (C2)
'   the order it landed in ............ _spec/_plans/tui-upgrades-delivery.puml (W12)
'   the live line it is built on ...... _spec/internal/ui/output-vocabulary.puml
'   teardown's steps, the first user .. _spec/internal/backend/teardown.puml (T6)
'   the page that names the steps ..... _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml (on enter)
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT WAS THERE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Teardown showed its running step as one live line with a clock (T6). The
' code lived in the sandbox backend. init's apply and a run's start printed a
' line when a step ENDED, so a slow download or a slow `sbx diagnose` looked
' like a hang.
'
' ── ONE RENDERER, IN ui ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' ui.Running(frame, plain) is T6's loop, moved: on a terminal one live line,
' redrawn every StepClock with frame(elapsed) and erased at the end; on any
' other output the plain line, once. Teardown's showStep now calls it with
' its own frame (place, name, clock, ceiling).
' ui.Steps is a plan of N steps over it:
'   Do(name, fn)     a live line: "step 2/5 · download sbx 0.49.2 · 12s"
'   Hand(name, fn)   a start line only: "step 3/5 · sign in to Docker"
'   Start(name)      the start line; the caller runs and records the step
'   DoAs · HandAs · StartAs   the same, with the line that stays unnumbered
' Each Do and Hand writes two rows to the run log, in teardown's format:
'   step: <name> started
'   step: <name> <duration> ok | failed: <first line of the error>
' A FINISHED Do LEAVES NO LINE ON A TERMINAL. What the step printed stays;
' its frame is erased, as teardown's are.
' A plan that runs past its count widens the total, so a line never reads
' "step 6/5". A nil plan runs its steps and shows nothing.
' STILL ONE LINE, NOT A TABLE. The delivery plan calls these "step tables".
' T6 landed as a line under the Printer's lock (teardown.puml records why),
' and W-k was written to build on T6's renderer. A table of done, running
' and pending rows was not built.
'
' ── A STEP THAT GIVES THE TERMINAL AWAY (W-o) ──────────────────────────────
' A live line is redrawn by a clock. Anything else drawing on the terminal
' at the same time gets that line written into it.
' MEASURED on tmux, 2026-11-11, with the code as W5 left it: a question
' opened while a step's line ticked, and the line drew over the question
' within 500 ms. That is teardown's pushed-branch question, behind the
' "pushed branches" step, since T6.
' TWO RULES NOW:
'   a prompt of proveo's own   choiceui.openTerminal calls ui.SuspendLive
'                              and resumes when the prompt closes. Every
'                              form, page, list and dialog opens through
'                              it, so none has to remember.
'   another program            the step is a Hand: a start line, no clock.
' SuspendLive erases the line and counts holders. While any holds, frames
' are stored and not drawn, and an ordinary line neither erases nor redraws
' the frame. The last resume draws the latest frame.
' The plan's wording was "ends the list's Program and starts a new one after
' it". There is no Program, so the line is taken off and put back.
' [Inference] A program proveo starts outside a Hand step, with a live line
' up, would still be drawn over. None is known: the three live-line steps of
' init, and the two of a run's start, start no terminal program.
'
' ── init's APPLY IS A LIST BEFORE IT IS A RUN (W-j, W-k) ───────────────────
' applyPlan(decisions, ctx) returns what setup's Enter runs, in order, each
' with a name, whether it gives the terminal away, and the func that runs
' it. Two readers use the one list:
'   the setup page   lists the names under "on enter" as the answers change
'   runApply         runs them, numbered, and stops at the first failure
' So the page cannot promise a step the apply does not run.
'   download sbx <release> | download the distro package        live
'   install sbx into <prefix> | install the distro package      hand
'   add <dir> to PATH        only when it will write the rc     live
'   sign in to Docker (sbx login)                               hand
'   run sbx's first-run wizard (sbx setup)                      hand
'   bind the network baseline: <name>                           hand
'   set the sandbox git identity      it can ask for a name     hand
'   install the prompt kit            it can ask what draws     hand
'   connect GitHub                    gh, then two forms        hand
'   verify sbx (sbx diagnose)         always                    live
' The PATH check still runs when it will only print; it is then no step.
' install() and installPackage() each split in two, so the download has a
' clock and the installer, which writes to the terminal itself, does not.
'
' ── A RUN'S START (W-k; R1 of output-readability, 2026-11-11) ──────────────
' sandbox.Run shows five steps before the agent has the terminal:
'   workload kit           live
'   stale sandbox check    live; hand only when a stale sandbox exists, since
'                          then it can ask and retiring runs steps of its own
'   sandbox secrets        live; it prints nothing while it runs, and each
'                          secret it stored becomes a "secret" row of the
'                          sbx block's one Facts block after it (R1 round 3)
'   create sandbox         hand, line "sbx create": `sbx create` writes to the
'                          terminal itself. A kept sandbox counts the step as
'                          "re-attach to <name> — left by an earlier run"; an
'                          OpenCode engine this run just created, "attach to
'                          <name>"
'   start <target>         the start line "<target> <version> — starting";
'                          the existing `agent` row records it
' A LINE THAT STAYS ON SCREEN CARRIES NO PLACE. DoAs, HandAs and StartAs take
' the line to show; the live frame keeps "step n/N · name · 12s", and each
' writes "step n/N · name" to the run log alone, so the log keeps the place.
' Plain output (a pipe, CI) gets the same unnumbered lines, so it never mixes
' the two forms. init keeps Do and Hand: its e2e reads "step n/N".
' A LIVE STEP DRAWS ITS PENDING HEADING FIRST. Do writes the place and
' "step: <name> started" to the log alone before its live frame would draw
' the heading, so the log read "step 1/5 · workload kit" under "workspace"
' and "sbx" mid-step (R1 review). Steps.do now calls Printer.heading before
' it logs; screen order is unchanged (TestALiveStepDrawsThePendingHeadingBeforeItsLogLines).
' The stale step's retire prints its own lines without "n/3" (kit-lifecycle.puml).
' The run log gains the first four rows ahead of `agent`, so one log now
' names every step of a run in order. The clone e2e compares that list.
' NOT WRAPPED: what run.Do does before sandbox.Run (image preflight, the
' local-model pull, the host add-ons). The pull draws a live line of its
' own, and two clocks on one line would take turns. A host add-on draws
' "<add-on> — starting" the same way (run.startAddon); in plain output it
' writes that line to the run log only, so nothing stays under egress.
' THE SBX INSTALL LINE reads "sbx — installing" or "sbx — upgrading", the
' command dim under it; installVerb gives each verb its own -ing form
' ("upgradeing" before R1 round 3; TestTheSbxInstallLineGivesEachVerbItsOwnIngForm).
'
' ── WHAT RAN ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' macOS and linux/arm64 on tmux: the setup page lists what Enter runs, the
' count follows "enter accept", and the apply prints a numbered line for
' each handed step and leaves none for a live one. A ticking step line stays
' off a question for 500 ms and returns after it; that test fails on the
' code without the suspend.
' macOS, real sandboxes: the clone run's log holds the four start rows, then
' `agent`, then teardown's nine. The Ctrl+C dialog still passes over a real
' agent, and over the fake sbx for the three harnesses whose image this host
' holds; the other seven skip.
' NOT RUN: an install from the network. Every init test finds the stub sbx
' already installed, so "download" and "install" ran in no test. Their names
' and order are unit-tested; their output on a terminal is not.
'
' Pinned by internal/ui/steps_test.go:
'   TestAStepShowsItsPlaceItsNameAndAClockThenLeavesNoLine
'   TestAHandedStepPrintsOneStartLineAndNoLiveFrame
'   TestPlainOutputGetsAStartLinePerStep
'   TestANilPlanRunsItsStepsAndShowsNothing
'   TestAPlanThatRunsPastItsCountNeverShowsAStepBeyondTheTotal
'   TestASuspendedLiveLineStaysOffTheTerminalUntilItIsResumed
'   TestAnOrdinaryLineUnderASuspendedLiveLineNeitherErasesNorRedrawsIt
'   TestAnAsStepLeavesItsOwnLineAndLogsItsPlace
'   TestPlainOutputOfAsStepsCarriesNoPlace
' Pinned by cmd/proveo/init_apply_test.go:
'   TestTheApplyPlanListsWhatEnterRunsInTheOrderItRuns
'   TestOnlyStepsThatKeepTheTerminalGetALiveLine
'   TestAnApplyNumbersItsListedStepsAndStopsAtTheFirstFailure
' Pinned by e2e: TestALiveStepLineStaysOffAQuestionAndComesBackAfterIt,
'   TestInitSaysWhatEnterRunsThenShowsEachStep,
'   TestCloneModeLandsTheCloneAndLiftsTheOutputDir (the log's step order)

component "ui.Running\na live line with a clock" as RUN <<app>>
component "ui.Steps\nstep n/N · name" as STEPS <<app>>
component "teardown\nnine steps, each with a ceiling" as TD <<app>>
component "init's apply\napplyPlan: one list, two readers" as INIT <<app>>
component "a run's start\nfive steps before the agent" as START <<app>>
component "a prompt of proveo's own\nform · page · list · dialog" as ASK <<host>>
component "another program\nsbx login · sbx create · a package manager" as OTHER <<cloud>>
component "**the line drawn over a question**" as OVER <<error>>

TD ARROW_MAIN RUN
STEPS ARROW_MAIN RUN
INIT ARROW_MAIN STEPS
START ARROW_MAIN STEPS
ASK ARROW_QUEUE RUN : SuspendLive, then resume
OTHER ARROW_OPTIONAL STEPS : Hand — a start line, no clock
RUN ARROW_ERROR OVER : what the suspend ended

note bottom of RUN
  **Erased when the step ends.** A terminal gets
  one line that redraws each second. A pipe or
  a log gets the plain line once, because it
  cannot redraw.
end note

note bottom of INIT
  **The page and the apply read one list.** The
  setup page names what Enter runs from the
  same plan the apply executes, so it cannot
  promise a step that does not run.
end note

note bottom of ASK
  **None has to remember.** Every prompt opens
  the terminal through one function. It takes
  the line off first and puts the latest
  frame back when the prompt closes.
end note

note bottom of OVER
  **Measured, then fixed.** Teardown's question
  about pushed branches opened behind a
  ticking line. On tmux the line drew over it
  inside half a second.
end note

note bottom of OTHER
  **No clock while it holds the terminal.** A
  step that starts a program which writes to
  the terminal prints its place once and
  waits.
end note

note bottom of START
  **One log names the whole run.** The start
  steps log in teardown's format, ahead of
  the agent's row. The clone e2e holds the
  order.
end note
@enduml
